      <main id="content"><article class="proof-reader" data-authored-declaration="AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GibbsLinearCovarianceUpper.gibbs_linear_covariance_upper"><div class="eyebrow">Samplinglib mathematical lesson</div><h1>Actual Gibbs linear covariance upper</h1><p><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GibbsLinearCovarianceUpper.gibbs_linear_covariance_upper</code> · theorem · <a href="index.html">Teaching coverage</a></p><section class="reader-first-pass" aria-label="First reading"><div class="reader-first-pass-label">Read this first</div><h2>Mathematical statement</h2><p class="reader-claim">For each direction a, the genuine covariance bilinear form of the normalized BOTH-curvature Gibbs law satisfies Cov_mu(a,a)&lt;=norma^2/m, using the actual linear observable, constant gradient and proven C1 Poincare.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation reader-main-equation">\[\mu=Z^{-1}e^{-W}dx,\quad mI\preceq D^2W\preceq MI,\quad X\in L^2(\mu)\Longrightarrow \operatorname{Cov}_\mu(a,a)\le \|a\|^2/m.\]</div><h3>Proof roadmap</h3><ol class="proof-roadmap"><li><span>1</span><strong>Normalize the actual Gibbs measure</strong><p>True exponential integrability gives probability. The canonical moment premise is real vectorL2, rather than a certificate of a covariance estimate.</p></li><li><span>2</span><strong>Take the genuine linear observable</strong><p>The continuous linear functional f(x)=inner(a,x) is C1. Actual vectorL2 yields scalarL2 by MemLp.const_inner.</p></li><li><span>3</span><strong>Identify its actual gradient</strong><p>The real Riesz isometry and true continuous-linear derivative show gradientf is constanta. It therefore has genuine weighted vectorL2.</p></li><li><span>4</span><strong>Use the proved curvature Poincare producer</strong><p>The accepted original-gradient/C1 theorem derives actual integrability and m*variance&lt;=energy, using BOTH curvature bounds. Poincare.Satisfies is not assumed.</p></li><li><span>5</span><strong>Preserve exact normalization</strong><p>The genuine constant gradient and probability mass1 make the Dirichlet integral exactly norma^2, with no missing energy prefactor.</p></li><li><span>6</span><strong>Bridge actual covariance and variance</strong><p>covarianceBilin_self requires the real vectorL2 premise; variance_eq_integral matches the genuine centered-square definition. Divide by positivem.</p></li></ol></section><details class="reader-ledger assumption-ledger"><summary>Full assumptions and notation</summary><h3>All objects and hypotheses</h3><ul><li>Finite real Hilbert/Borel full E including0, actual C2 W, true exp(-W) volume integrability and positive partition, BOTH global mI&lt;=HessW&lt;=MI with0&lt;m&lt;=M.</li><li>Genuine vector id in L2 of normalized tilted Gibbs law. This canonical node keeps the moment premise explicit to rule out totalized covariance outside its integrable domain; the actual paper consumer produces it internally. No covariance/Poincare certificate input.</li></ul><p class="muted"></p></details><h2>Mathematical proof</h2><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>1. Normalize the actual Gibbs measure</h4><p>True exponential integrability gives probability. The canonical moment premise is real vectorL2, rather than a certificate of a covariance estimate.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\mu=Z^{-1}e^{-W}dx,\quad \mu(E)=1,\quad X\in L^2(\mu).\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>isProbabilityMeasure_tilted</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>2. Take the genuine linear observable</h4><p>The continuous linear functional f(x)=inner(a,x) is C1. Actual vectorL2 yields scalarL2 by MemLp.const_inner.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[f_a(x)=\langle a,x\rangle,\quad f_a\in C^1\cap L^2(\mu).\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>ContinuousLinearMap.contDiff; MemLp.const_inner</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>3. Identify its actual gradient</h4><p>The real Riesz isometry and true continuous-linear derivative show gradientf is constanta. It therefore has genuine weighted vectorL2.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\nabla f_a(x)=a,\quad\nabla f_a\in L^2(\mu).\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>toDual_gradient; ContinuousLinearMap.fderiv; memLp_const</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>4. Use the proved curvature Poincare producer</h4><p>The accepted original-gradient/C1 theorem derives actual integrability and m*variance&lt;=energy, using BOTH curvature bounds. Poincare.Satisfies is not assumed.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[m\operatorname{Var}_\mu(f_a)\le\int\|\nabla f_a\|^2d\mu.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>GibbsC1Poincare.gibbs_c1_variance_poincare</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>5. Preserve exact normalization</h4><p>The genuine constant gradient and probability mass1 make the Dirichlet integral exactly norma^2, with no missing energy prefactor.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\int\|\nabla f_a\|^2d\mu=\|a\|^2.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>integral_const; probReal_univ; Poincare.dirichletEnergy</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>6. Bridge actual covariance and variance</h4><p>covarianceBilin_self requires the real vectorL2 premise; variance_eq_integral matches the genuine centered-square definition. Divide by positivem.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\operatorname{Cov}_\mu(a,a)=\operatorname{Var}_\mu(f_a)\le\|a\|^2/m.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>covarianceBilin_self; variance_eq_integral; le_div_iff₀</p></details></div><section class="lean-verification"><h2>Lean verification</h2><p>The exact proposition and proof begin folded so the mathematical argument remains the primary reading path.</p><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-statement" data-inline-lean="AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GibbsLinearCovarianceUpper.gibbs_linear_covariance_upper"><summary>Lean statement · gibbs_linear_covariance_upper</summary><p>For each direction a, the genuine covariance bilinear form of the normalized BOTH-curvature Gibbs law satisfies Cov_mu(a,a)&lt;=norma^2/m, using the actual linear observable, constant gradient and proven C1 Poincare.</p><p>Braces mark parameters Lean can infer; square brackets request structures such as a measurable space or probability measure. Named hypotheses are mathematical premises, not facts established by this declaration. Section parameters are described in the mathematical hypotheses above; the module link retains their exact source context.</p><pre class="code-block"><code class="language-lean">theorem gibbs_linear_covariance_upper
    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E] [CompleteSpace E]
    (W : E → ℝ) (hW : ContDiff ℝ 2 W)
    (hI : Integrable (fun x =&gt; Real.exp (-W x)))
    (hZ : 0 &lt; ∫ x, Real.exp (-W x))
    (m M : ℝ) (hm : 0 &lt; m) (hmM : m ≤ M)
    (hlower : ∀ x a, m*‖a‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ W) x a a)
    (hupper : ∀ x a, fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ W) x a a ≤ M*‖a‖^2)
    (hX : MemLp id 2 ((volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x =&gt; -W x))) :
    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x =&gt; -W x)
    ∀ a : E, ProbabilityTheory.covarianceBilin μ a a ≤ ‖a‖^2/m</code></pre><p><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-functionalinequalities-gibbslinearcovarianceupper.html#complete-module-source">Exact module and namespace context</a></p></details><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-proof" data-inline-lean="AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GibbsLinearCovarianceUpper.gibbs_linear_covariance_upper"><summary>Lean proof · gibbs_linear_covariance_upper</summary><p>Normalize the actual Gibbs measure; Take the genuine linear observable; Identify its actual gradient; Use the proved curvature Poincare producer; Preserve exact normalization; Bridge actual covariance and variance</p><p>Braces mark parameters Lean can infer; square brackets request structures such as a measurable space or probability measure. Named hypotheses are mathematical premises, not facts established by this declaration. Section parameters are described in the mathematical hypotheses above; the module link retains their exact source context.</p><pre class="code-block"><code class="language-lean">theorem gibbs_linear_covariance_upper
    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E] [CompleteSpace E]
    (W : E → ℝ) (hW : ContDiff ℝ 2 W)
    (hI : Integrable (fun x =&gt; Real.exp (-W x)))
    (hZ : 0 &lt; ∫ x, Real.exp (-W x))
    (m M : ℝ) (hm : 0 &lt; m) (hmM : m ≤ M)
    (hlower : ∀ x a, m*‖a‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ W) x a a)
    (hupper : ∀ x a, fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ W) x a a ≤ M*‖a‖^2)
    (hX : MemLp id 2 ((volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x =&gt; -W x))) :
    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x =&gt; -W x)
    ∀ a : E, ProbabilityTheory.covarianceBilin μ a a ≤ ‖a‖^2/m := by
  let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x =&gt; -W x)
  let : IsProbabilityMeasure μ := isProbabilityMeasure_tilted hI
  dsimp only
  intro a
  let f : E → ℝ := fun x =&gt; inner ℝ a x
  have hf : ContDiff ℝ 1 f := (innerSL ℝ a).contDiff
  have hp : MemLp f 2 μ := hX.const_inner a
  have hgrad : gradient f = fun _ =&gt; a := by
    funext x
    apply (toDual ℝ E).injective
    rw [toDual_gradient]
    exact (innerSL ℝ a).fderiv
  have hq : MemLp (gradient f) 2 μ := hgrad ▸ memLp_const a
  obtain ⟨_, hb⟩ := GibbsC1Poincare.gibbs_c1_variance_poincare
    W hW hI hZ m M hm hmM hlower hupper f hf hp hq
  have henergy : Poincare.dirichletEnergy μ f = ‖a‖^2 := by
    simp only [Poincare.dirichletEnergy, hgrad]
    simp
  rw [henergy] at hb
  have hcov : covarianceBilin μ a a = Poincare.variance μ f := by
    rw [covarianceBilin_self hX a, variance_eq_integral hp.aemeasurable]
    rfl
  rw [hcov]
  exact (le_div_iff₀ hm).2 (by simpa only [mul_comm] using hb)

end
end AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GibbsLinearCovarianceUpper</code></pre><p><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-functionalinequalities-gibbslinearcovarianceupper.html#complete-module-source">Exact module and namespace context</a></p></details></section><details class="reader-ledger boundary-ledger"><summary>Scope and omitted-condition boundaries</summary><ul><li>Canonical BOTH-curvature Gibbs linear covariance upper with genuine vectorL2, actual positive partition and probability normalization; not full anisotropic Brascamp-Lieb. Actual source beta=1 alpha=kappa^-1, 1&lt;=kappa, 0&lt;eta&lt;=1; genuine posterior law R_y, internally produced probability/vectorL2/positive partitions/C2 and normalized-U versus unnormalized-V_eta constant shift. Derive true covariance upper and both Hessian bounds (kappa+eta)^-1 and (1+eta)^-1, then true 1-Lipschitz gradient. Finite real Hilbert/Borel including zero dimension is disclosed representation extension. No input covariance/PI/oracle/moment/normalizer certificate on source Anchor. No joint measurable posterior kernel selector, higher smoothing derivatives, algorithm/Wp/proxy-warmness/main/querycost/composition. PBPS reflected quarter law and source-score remain separate. TV never transfers unbounded expected cost.</li></ul></details><details class="proof-reader-provenance reader-ledger"><summary>Sources, dependencies, and reuse</summary><h2>Source and reuse</h2><h3>Samplinglib parents called</h3><ul><li><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-functionalinequalities-gibbsc1poincare.html#decl-autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-functionalinequalities-gibbsc1poincar-beafcfbb8f"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GibbsC1Poincare.gibbs_c1_variance_poincare</code></a></li></ul><h3>Mathlib API called (external library)</h3><ul><li>covarianceBilin_self</li><li>variance_eq_integral</li><li>MemLp.const_inner</li><li>toDual_gradient</li><li>ContinuousLinearMap.fderiv</li><li>integral_const</li><li>le_div_iff₀</li></ul><h3>Mathematical sources</h3><ul><li><a href="https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.Thmtheorem1">SPHMC actual Lemma4.1 and explicit covariance prerequisite</a> — Canonical BOTH-curvature Gibbs linear covariance upper with genuine vectorL2, actual positive partition and probability normalization; not full anisotropic Brascamp-Lieb. Actual source beta=1 alpha=kappa^-1, 1&lt;=kappa, 0&lt;eta&lt;=1; genuine posterior law R_y, internally produced probability/vectorL2/positive partitions/C2 and normalized-U versus unnormalized-V_eta constant shift. Derive true covariance upper and both Hessian bounds (kappa+eta)^-1 and (1+eta)^-1, then true 1-Lipschitz gradient. Finite real Hilbert/Borel including zero dimension is disclosed representation extension. No input covariance/PI/oracle/moment/normalizer certificate on source Anchor. No joint measurable posterior kernel selector, higher smoothing derivatives, algorithm/Wp/proxy-warmness/main/querycost/composition. PBPS reflected quarter law and source-score remain separate. TV never transfers unbounded expected cost.</li></ul><p>Samplinglib prose is not a quotation or a source-equivalence certificate. Definitions and aliases are explained as constructions, not counted as new mathematical proofs.</p></details></article></main>
